WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.460
The terrorist attacks
of September 11, 2001

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.660
continue to cast a long
shadow over American life.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.630
20 years later,

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:08.670
at home and abroad,

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.030
the world is more chaotic and less free

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.550
because the U.S. government
exploited our fears

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.870
to erode our liberties

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.930
and launch two disastrous foreign wars.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.060
This is an attack

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.880
on all that America is.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.850
Every nation must take seriously,

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.570
the growing threat of terror
on a catastrophic scale.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.320
Can we ever feel safe again?

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.460
Even just like the feeling of security,

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.700
I think is so important.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.189
War has been declared...

00:00:33.189 --> 00:00:34.930
Bill, you've got to
unleash the dogs of war.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.789
Either you're with us,

00:00:36.789 --> 00:00:39.490
or you are with the terrorists.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.050
Today's defining crisis,

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.080
the COVID-19 pandemic, has created

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.230
another opportunity to restrict freedom

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.710
in the name of protecting
us from a fearsome enemy.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.580
In this case,

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.717
a viral infection.

00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:51.515
The breaking news, stay at home.

00:00:51.515 --> 00:00:52.550
That is the order tonight.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.580
These are people who are frightened

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.470
Stay home and stay away from others.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.110
Certain amount of arm twisting

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.650
by governments is perfectly justified.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.050
If everything is reopened,

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:03.810
then what's the carrot going to be?

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.690
I wasn't thinking of the bill
of rights when we did this

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.890
So what will the world look like

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.080
20 years from now?

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.800
9/11 led to illegal detentions, torture,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.700
routine warrantless spying
on everyday Americans,

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.214
two wars, and an explosion
of government spending.

00:01:18.214 --> 00:01:20.630
COVID-19 has brought
unconstitutional restrictions

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.550
on travel between states and cities,

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.320
vaccine and mask mandates,

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.180
lockdown orders that closed businesses,

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.710
schools, and churches,

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.960
restrictions on dining in restaurants

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.300
and exercising in gyms,

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.650
and an explosion of government spending.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:34.800
Early in the pandemic,

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.920
President Trump invoked
the Defense Production Act

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.920
to compel businesses

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.870
to produce ventilators and other supplies

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.340
for combating the virus

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.350
when the federal government
didn't like the terms offered

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.400
after 9/11,

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.750
Congress created the
Department of Homeland Security

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.850
and nationalized airport
security by creating the TSA.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.270
The federal government also

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.940
conscripted communications companies

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.400
into monitoring customers,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.880
even going so far as to install

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.750
National Security Agency
equipment in AT&amp;T facilities.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.870
Politicians seem to understand
instinctively that a crisis

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.380
is an opening to push
freedom eroding policies

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.900
previously too hard to
get the public to accept.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.570
Such as the disastrous war in Iraq,

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.350
which had nothing to do with the attacks.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:13.870
But regime change in Iraq

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:14.960
had been on the wishlist of

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:18.140
senior Bush administration
officials long before 9/11

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.376
and the terrorist attack
created an opening.

00:02:20.376 --> 00:02:21.717
You're going to get him out of there?

00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:22.958
I'd like to, of course,

00:02:22.958 --> 00:02:24.970
and I presume this
administration would as well.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.480
For then Senator Biden,

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.070
the 9/11 attacks provided

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.740
an opening for railroading
through Congress

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:30.950
a bill that he had drafted

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.080
following the Oklahoma city bombing,

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.630
but that he couldn't get passed.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.550
It became the Patriot act.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.690
Almost the same thing that got passed,

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:39.620
The Patriot Act,

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.300
was introduced by me in 1994.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.000
And it was the right
wing that defeated it.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.130
20 years later,

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.550
even while correctly predicting

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.630
that the Supreme court
would overturn the order.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.010
President Biden extended

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.370
an emergency federal eviction moratorium,

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:55.520
that was always based on faulty science,

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.560
violating the property rights
of millions of landlords.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.520
September 11th reminds
us that dressed policies

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:02.740
and accumulated authority

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.710
have a nasty way of lingering
long after the emergencies

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:07.630
for which they were invoked
have come to an end.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.310
It created an opportunity

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.250
for new government spending on initiatives

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.690
that had little to do with
keeping Americans safe.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:16.650
Congress diverted billions
of dollars to often wasteful

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.510
"homeland security" spending,

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.030
including counter-terrorism
funding for small towns,

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.550
hundreds of miles from
major American cities.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.290
Why would Al Qaeda to come Tiptonville?

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.980
If I were Al Qaeda,

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.990
and I wanted to get Memphis,

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.940
I'd come to Tiptonville.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.920
No one would ever expect me here.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:35.550
As 60 Minutes reported in 2005,

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.800
the money was spent on
transporting lawnmowers

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.050
to lawnmower races, Segways,
air conditioned garbage trucks,

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:45.090
bulletproof dog vests,
and decontamination units

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.940
nobody knew how to operate.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:49.020
The people who view these as not necessary

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.410
I think are wrong.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.980
Today's proverbial crisis

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.400
that's too good to waste

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.990
has led to trillions in
passed or proposed spending

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.150
for so-called recovery and infrastructure.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.150
Somehow that's been defined
to include internet access,

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:04.660
child tax credits, electric
vehicle charging stations,

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.730
corporate subsidies, and
buy American mandates,

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:10.150
Everything, it turns out,
is a necessary expense

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.400
for fighting COVID-19 when
politicians see opportunity.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.530
20 years from now,

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:17.290
we may well still be
living with crippling debt,

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.960
"emergency" government programs

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.740
that somehow were never phased out

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.470
and pandemic fueled
restrictions on our daily lives.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:26.240
Or we'll look back at the
pandemic as a turning point

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.260
in which Americans
rediscovered their ability

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.820
to move past a crisis and reclaim control

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.150
over their own lives,

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:35.000
if we can break the
pattern set after 9/11,

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.960
the 20 year anniversary of
September 11, 2001 is a day

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.960
for mourning the loss of
the nearly 3000 people

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.780
who perished tragically
on that horrific day

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.480
and to dwell on how
political leaders used fear

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:48.900
to steal our liberties,

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.810
because history is already
repeating itself in ways

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:55.093
that we and our kids will live to regret.

